e0a4f6d1-0b9f-47cc-844c-2b0101d586ac	ULAW 2100	Access to Justice	19747793-3475-4bf5-b85f-dffefe2f5a13	How do lower-income people navigate and experience the civil and criminal legal systems? This course will consider what "access to justice" means and requires, both for the structure of our legal systems and at a practical level. Students will be introduced to a range of topics that may include the right to counsel, the role of non-lawyers, the use of technology, legal design, and legal literacy. Prerequisite/Corequisite: ULAW 1000 Introduction to American Law. [3]	3	\N	0	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-20 05:56:40.53763+00	2026-02-20 05:56:40.53763+00
1e8d8a6b-0fbd-491c-98e5-fc9fb2ac913b	ULAW 2540	International Protection of Human Rights	19747793-3475-4bf5-b85f-dffefe2f5a13	This course will study the rules, institutions, and legal theories that seek to protect basic liberties for all people in connection with the interrelated field of international humanitarian law. The course will emphasize (1) specific "hot button" subjects within human rights law (including the death penalty, hate speech, refugee rights, and gender rights); (2) judicial and legislative authorities that interpret and implement legal rules relating to these subjects; and (3) public and private actors who seek redress for those whose rights have been violated. Prerequisite/Corequisite: ULAW 1000 Introduction to American Law. [3]	3	\N	0	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-20 05:56:40.539499+00	2026-02-20 05:56:40.539499+00
94b5df1a-fea7-4eb3-a150-a387dc269625	ULAW 2542	Introduction to Artificial Intelligence in the Legal Profession	19747793-3475-4bf5-b85f-dffefe2f5a13	This course provides a broad survey of artificial intelligence technology and its relationship to law and legal practice. Students will gain foundational knowledge of AI systems and explore their applications across various areas of legal work. The course examines ethical considerations, legal challenges, and current regulatory developments in AI and law. Designed for students without technical backgrounds and builds AI/legal literacy from introductory concepts, preparing students to adapt to continued evolution in this field. [3]	3	\N	0	\N	\N	\N	2026-02-20 05:56:40.541476+00	2026-02-20 05:56:40.541476+00
